    "input_head": "Here are our documents.\n\n=== FY26 Program Report ===\nIn fiscal year 2026, Harborlight enrolled 1,148 adult learners across five neighborhood sites, up from 936 the year before. Of those learners, 412 were working toward a high school equivalency credential and 389 were English language learners.\nSixty-eight percent of learners who stayed at least 12 weeks gained one or more reading levels on the CASAS assessment. Seventy-one learners earned a high school equivalency credential, the most in the organization's history.\n\nA corps of 214 volunteer tutors gave 9,870 tutoring hours. The average tutor stayed 14 months. Harborlight employs 11 full-time staff, including four site coordinators.\n\nOperating expenses for FY2026 were $1,420,000. Program costs were 81 percent of spending. Foundation grants provided $640,000, individual donors gave $388,000, and the city's adult education contract paid $295,000.\nThe cost per learner was $1,237.\n\nAt year end, 287 adults were on the waitlist, most of them at the Eastgate and Riverside sites. The average wait was nine weeks.\n\nStaff recommend that the board approve an FY2027 budget of $1,610,000, which adds a sixth site at the Eastgate branch library and two site coordinators. Staff estimate the sixth site would serve 180 more learners a year and cut the waitlist in half.\n“I read my granddaughter a bedtime story for the first time this spring,” said a learner at the Riverside site.\n\n=== Board retreat notes ===\nBoard retreat notes, September 13\n\nP"
  },
